### R1-CORR-003: cold-start path silently enables required-check on wrapperless repo

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh `check_forward_mode_safety()` lines 511-529 (cold-start branch under NO_PRIOR_GREEN_CI=1). When the wrapper workflow is absent (workflow_id empty), the run-count block at lines 513-525 is skipped, and the function falls through to line 527-528 (`log 'safety check bypassed'; return 0`). This allows enabling the required-check on a repo that has never had the wrapper wired up, locking ALL future PRs with a check that can never pass. The normal path at lines 531-535 errors explicitly when workflow_id is empty; the cold-start path lacks this guard.

**Fix:** Add an absent-workflow guard at the start of the cold-start path (after fetching workflow_id at line 512, before the `if [ -n "$workflow_id" ]` block). Pattern: if workflow_id is empty, error with a message that distinguishes from the normal path (cold-start adopters still need the wrapper workflow file in their repo before the script will enable required-check). Example diagnostic: `error: --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci requires the wrapper workflow file '$WORKFLOW_LOOKUP_PATH' to be present in ${REPO}; add the wrapper PR first` → exit 2.

**Test:** Add a test case in tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh near the existing cold-start tests. Pattern:
```bash
repo_dir="$TMPDIR/enable-cold-start-no-wrapper"
init_case_repo "$repo_dir"
fake_gh_dir="$TMPDIR/fake-gh-enable-cold-start-no-wrapper"
make_restore_fake_gh "$fake_gh_dir"
cat >"$fake_gh_dir/repo.json" <<'EOF'
{"default_branch":"main"}
EOF
cat >"$fake_gh_dir/workflows.json" <<'EOF'
{"workflows":[]}
EOF
commit_case "$repo_dir" "enable cold-start no wrapper"
run_enable_case "$repo_dir" "$fake_gh_dir" 2 '' 'wrapper workflow file' --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci
```
Adjust the diagnostic match string to match the actual error text in your edit.

### R1-SB-002: §12.8 Gate 3 SOP missing post-extended-breakage cold-start flag note

**Bug:** docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.8 Gate 3 RE-ENABLE block shows the plain `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch>` command with no conditional guidance. When the adopter's wrapper has been broken for >60 days (a realistic post-extended-breakage scenario), the forward-mode safety check at scripts/enable-required-check.sh line 544 (`if [ "$run_count" -eq 0 ]`) exits 2 with the cold-start-only diagnostic. Operator under break-glass time pressure may misuse `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` semantically (it's named for cold-start) or abandon Gate 3, leaving the primitive permanently disabled.

**Fix:** Add one sentence to docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.8 Gate 3, after the basic re-enable command block, before the CAUTION callout. Suggested wording: 'If the wrapper has had no successful runs in the past 60 days due to extended pre-Gate-2 breakage, append `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` to bypass the cold-start safety check (the flag's name is from the cold-start case; semantically it gates the same condition).' (Adjust phrasing to match surrounding doc voice.)

