{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '54,66p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md && printf '\\\\n----\\\\n' && sed -n '94,112p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md && printf '\\\\n----\\\\n' && sed -n '90,105p' docs/DECISIONS.md && printf '\\\\n----\\\\n' && sed -n '150,170p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n----\\\\n' && sed -n '314,326p' STATUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n## Carry-forward known findings (from extras-parking r8-archive)\n\nThese were surfaced in extras-parking R8 but not closed at parking time. Address proactively in this slice:\n\n1. **R8-SAFE-001** (extras-parking): `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is a backdoor; D-044 trust-model claim 'Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent' becomes inaccurate when bypassed. Mitigation: WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.\n2. **R8-SAFE-002** (extras-parking): Gate 3 forward-mode prior-entry detection misses uncommitted Gate-1 entries. Mitigation: also check working-tree diff via `git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md`.\n3. **R8 Bootstrap** (extras-parking): workflow self-blocks introducing slice's own PR. **CLOSED in 024B-extras** via `paths:` whitelist `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` (cohort-only trigger; naturally excludes `024[AB]` slice prefixes) + explicit `branch-protection-log.md` / `STATUS.md` triggers + job-body short-circuit on tooling slices or missing cascade-slice DISPATCH-NOTE.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `--restore` mode logic correct (GET→PUT transform; APPLY_FAIL; posture-degradation flags; required_signatures sub-resource; pre-restore state capture; restore log block).\n- [ ] Forward-mode safety check uses path-pinned workflow lookup (not display name) + no branch filter on workflow-runs API.\n\n----\n| 2 | Manual scope check + verify-commands | Opus | ~5 min |\n| 3 | 3× sequential Sonnet R1 review (64k cap) | Sonnet | ~30 min |\n| 4 | Fix-rounds (expected 1-2 for the smaller 024B-extras-1 surface) | Codex + Sonnet | variable |\n| 5 | **Operator-interactive `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo** | Operator interactive (gh PAT, throw-away test repo) | ~15 min |\n| 6 | Final R-fixpoint + self-merge | Opus | ~10 min |\n\nTarget: 024B-extras merged within ~3-4 hours wall-clock + operator demo gating window.\n\n## Reservation guard\n\nD-047 reserved for this slice. Codex must NOT assign D-047 to anything else.\n\n---\n\n**Status:** ACTIVE (post-024B-core merge). Awaiting operator-interactive step-7 evidence completion and R-fixpoint review.\n\n----\n| D-037 | 2026-05-01 | Grant `issues: write` permission to the `release-gate-violation-issue` job in `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` (per WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1, closing TF-020H3rg-003). Privilege scope is the JOB level (not workflow default); the release-gate evaluation job continues to run with `contents: read` only. The new job fires only on `needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'` — workflow_dispatch dry-runs and clean push:tags runs never reach it. The job's only mutation is `gh issue create` / `gh issue comment` / `gh label create --force` against the SCP source repo's own Issues namespace; no other write surface is unlocked. The auto-opened issue assigns `@jrnb2024` (single-operator mode per D-031); forward-compat env `SCP_RELEASE_GATE_ASSIGNEES` for 2nd-maintainer escalation. Symmetric with D-029 (020C.1 `statuses: write` for read-back commit-status) — a privilege-write expansion ratified by an amending decision row that names the precise threat-surface and bounded behaviour | ACCEPTED | The release-gate's last-line-of-defense alarm needs SOME write surface to surface beyond the workflow log; opening a GitHub issue is the lightest-weight signal that survives operator absence (the workflow log is ephemeral; the issue persists + assigns + sends a notification). Privilege-of-least-privilege is honoured by job-level scoping rather than workflow-level — the gate-evaluation steps (pip install, schema validate, ramp check, expired-config check) cannot accidentally open issues because they run in the release-gate job which has only `contents: read`. CODEOWNERS coverage on `.github/**` (per WP-SCP-020 020K) gates any change to release-gate.yml itself. The forward-compat env mirrors `SCP_REGRESSION_ASSIGNEES` from canary-replay.yml. Identified at WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1 R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 + SAFE-MAJ-001 closures |\n| D-038 | 2026-05-02 | Adopt hash-pinned Python supply-chain installs across the SCP federation primitive's two YAML/JSON-validating workflows (`.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` × 4 install sites, `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` × 1 install site) via `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`) match the prior inline pins exactly — no version bump on the public Python deps; only the install mechanism is hardened. Lockfile generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` from `requirements/policy-check.in`; full transitive closure (`attrs`, `jsonschema-specifications`, `referencing`, `rpds-py`) hash-pinned with all-platform wheel SHA256s. Closes WP-SCP-022 TF-020H3rg-002 (filed at 020H.3 R1 safety MIN-SAFE-006 — a PyPI compromise of either pinned version could substitute a malicious package on the next install; `--require-hashes` causes pip to refuse install when the served wheel's SHA256 is not in the lockfile). PATCH bump (v1.0.0 → v1.0.1) per `policies/VERSIONING.md` PATCH category (\"internal refactors of helpers/lib\"); no `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry required (no surface deprecation, no behaviour change for adopters). Lockfile regeneration command captured in `requirements/policy-check.txt` header AND `requirements/policy-check.in` documentation block | ACCEPTED | Symmetric supply-chain hardening with the pre-existing `scripts/scp-