into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\n\n> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\n\n----\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\n\n| # | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Slice 024B-extras: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore` added with GET-shape → PUT-shape transform, posture-degradation ack